ze2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>As always, these are my thoughts and opinions. Nothing more. Have a plan before you do anything, and you are responsible for your portfolio. Sometimes I take losses too…its apart of the game. But keep them small, and let your runners run. Feel free to ping me in the chat for any questions. </p><p></p><p> </p></li></ul>",
  "has_dynamic_content": false,
  "truncated_body_text": "As mentioned last week, we discussed adding positions (or adding to current positions) should they start performing. We are seeing that. We are also seeing a wide array of stocks up a healthy amount pre-market. The volatility index, VIX also came below 22…in fact, it gapped down, currently at 20.08. Could all of this change in a moment? Could a tweet come out and reverse everything negatively? Absolutely, hence why we focus more on risk management than on profits. Profits come in time. The market has been difficult, but we are up for the year. The patience has paid off and looking at various charts and signals,",
